## Codex Tool Usage

- Pass an explicit `workdir` to shell command tools.
- Use `rtk` for supported commands with token-heavy output. Use `rtk proxy` for required raw output and native commands for unsupported syntax.
- A `PreToolUse` hook denies `cat` of files over 350 lines. Read a bounded range with `sed -n`, or delegate the reading with `bulk-read` as described in the `my-bulk-read` skill.

## Codex Browser Routing

- For browser work, follow the `my-browser` skill.
- Use Computer Use only when the user explicitly requests it or the task needs a desktop app outside the browser.

## Codex Subagent Routing

- Set `fork_turns` explicitly: normally `"none"`; use `"all"` only when the task needs the full conversation. Use configured wait defaults instead of short status polling.
